// Undertaking Climax (D20), p.82-83.
(
    name: "Undertaking Climax",
    die: D20,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "A Hollow Victory", text: "You succeed. The monster is slain, the ritual is stopped, the sanctuary is cleansed. But in the process, the very thing you sought to protect is destroyed. The village is now a graveyard, the \"cure\" has rendered the patient a mindless husk, the \"safe haven\" is now a crater.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "The Cycle Continues", text: "The entity you defeated was not the source of the problem, merely a symptom. Its death sends out a silent call, and you know with chilling certainty that another will rise to take its place. You have not ended the threat, you have merely reset the clock.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "The Ultimate Sacrifice", text: "The only way to win is for one of you to make a terrible choice: merge with the Flesh to contain it, or absorb the Choir's curse into yourself. One hero must be lost to save the others.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "No Happy Endings", text: "Your victory creates a power vacuum. By destroying the local Choir presence, the Flesh in the region grows unchecked, and vice-versa. The survivors you \"saved\" are now at the mercy of a different, perhaps even worse, predator that you unleashed.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "Poisoned Knowledge", text: "You find the knowledge you sought, but the knowledge itself is corrupting. Knowing it invites nightmares, causes physical mutation, or acts as a beacon, drawing greater horrors towards you.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "The Ascension", text: "The final confrontation was a ritual, and you were the last component. By defeating the \"guardian\", you complete the ceremony. The antagonist doesn't die; it ascends, transforming into a far more powerful and terrifying entity, and it thanks you for your help.")),
        (7, 7, (title: "The Merger", text: "In its death throes, the Choir entity and the Flesh horror you were fighting merge into a single, new abomination. It possesses the intelligent malice of the Choir and the mindless hunger of the Flesh. You have created a perfect monster.")),
        (8, 8, (title: "The Personal Betrayal", text: "The person who sent you on this undertaking appears at the climax, revealing they manipulated you from the start. Your actions have weakened their rivals, secured a powerful artifact for them, or simply cleared the path for their own ascension. Your quest was a lie.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "Not What It Seems", text: "You learn that the \"monsters\" you've been fighting were actually protecting something; a fragile truce, a seal on an even older evil, a group of untainted children. By destroying them, you have broken the seal and doomed the innocent. You were the villains all along.")),
        (10, 10, (title: "The Pyrrhic Victory", text: "You win the final battle, but you are left irrevocably scarred. You are mutated, driven half-mad, or spiritually tainted. You are no longer fully human, and other survivors now look at you with the same fear they once reserved for the monsters.")),
        (11, 11, (title: "The False Dawn", text: "It's over. The threat is gone, the sun seems brighter. For the first time in ages, there is peace. This peace lasts for a day, maybe two. Then, the real threat, the one that used your previous foe as a pawn or a distraction, makes its move.")),
        (12, 12, (title: "The Pawn", text: "Your actions have perfectly fulfilled a dark prophecy. Every step you took, every monster you killed, was part of a cosmic chess game. You were not heroes; you were the instruments that allowed a greater, sleeping power to awaken.")),
        (13, 13, (title: "The Invitation", text: "The entity at the heart of your quest is not a mindless beast or a Choir zealot. It is an emissary for a third, unknown power; something from the stars, the sea, or a different reality. It judges you worthy and offers you a place in its coming apocalypse.")),
        (14, 14, (title: "Unwitting Betrayal", text: "The final confrontation reveals the source of the horror is one of the party members. A dormant mutation, a forgotten pact, or a cursed bloodline has been unconsciously fueling the local phenomena. To end it, they must be contained or destroyed.")),
        (15, 15, (title: "New Responsibilities", text: "You succeed, and a group of desperate, broken survivors now looks to you as their leaders. You are now responsible for their food, shelter, and safety. The adventure is over, but the crushing burden of leadership has just begun.")),
        (16, 16, (title: "Contagious Ideas", text: "The \"anti-hymn\" or heretical philosophy you've discovered works. It frees people from the Choir, but it is a memetic virus. It replaces faith with a violent, nihilistic rage, creating a new faction of murderous atheists who are just as dangerous as the monsters.")),
        (17, 17, (title: "The Undying Foe", text: "The final enemy cannot be killed. It is a concept, a recurring event, a force of nature. You can fight it off, banish it temporarily, but it will always return. The only true victory is to abandon the area and warn others that this place is eternally damned.")),
        (18, 18, (title: "A New Threat", text: "In defeating the local Choir/Flesh presence, you have upset a delicate, horrifying balance. The natural world, long dormant, awakens in a malevolent new way. The air is poison, the water is poison, the game is poison. Everything wants to kill you.")),
        (19, 19, (title: "The Broken Weapon", text: "The weapon or relic you needed to defeat the final boss is destroyed in the process. You are left victorious but disarmed, having sacrificed your greatest asset to survive this one encounter.")),
        (20, 20, (title: "The War is Upon You", text: "Your actions draw the attention of the wider War of the Millennium. By making a stand, you have planted a flag. Now, a full Choir legion and a massive Flesh Tide are converging on your location. You have not found an ending; you have found the front line.")),
    ],
)
